{"id": "haiku__GEN__omni_2056__3", "result": "**Setting up the equation.** Write $\\overline{ABC} = 100A + 10B + C$. The condition $\\overline{ABC} = B^C - A$ becomes\n\n$$B^C = 101A + 10B + C,$$\n\nwith $A \\in \\{1,\\dots,9\\}$ (since the number is three-digit), $B, C \\in \\{0,\\dots,9\\}$, and $B^C \\le 1008$.\n\n**Case analysis on $B$:**\n\n- **$B = 0$:** $0^C = 0$ (for $C \\ge 1$) or $1$ (for $C = 0$). Neither can equal $101A + C \\ge 101$. No solutions.\n- **$B = 1$:** $1^C = 1 < 101$. No solutions.\n- **$B = 2$:** Need $2^C - C - 20 = 101A$.\n  - $C \\le 4$: negative.\n  - $C=5$: $32-25=7$. No.\n  - $C=6$: $64-26=38$. No.\n  - $C=7$: $128-27=101$, so $A=1$. **Solution.**\n  - $C=8$: $256-28=228$. No.\n  - $C=9$: $512-29=483$. No.\n- **$B = 3$:** Need $3^C - C - 30 = 101A$.\n  - $C=4$: $81-34=47$. No.\n  - $C=5$: $243-35=208$. No.\n  - $C=6$: $729-36=693$. No.\n  - $C \\ge 7$: $3^7 = 2187 > 1008$.\n- **$B = 4$:** $4^3 - 43 = 21$, $4^4 - 44 = 212$, and $4^5 = 1024 > 1008$. No solutions.\n- **$B = 5$:** $5^3 - 53 = 72$, $5^4 - 54 = 571$, and $5^5 > 1008$. No solutions.\n- **$B = 6$:** $6^3 - 63 = 153$, and $6^4 > 1008$. No solutions.\n- **$B = 7$:** $7^3 - 73 = 270$, and $7^4 > 1008$. No solutions.\n- **$B = 8$:** $8^3 - 83 = 429$, and $8^4 > 1008$. No solutions.\n- **$B = 9$:** $9^3 - 93 = 636$, and $9^4 > 1008$. No solutions.\n\n**Check the solution:** $A=1, B=2, C=7$ gives $\\overline{ABC} = 127$, and $2^7 - 1 = 128 - 1 = 127$. \u2713\n\nANSWER: 127", "rc": 0, "cost": 0.0013231999999999999, "model_used": ["claude-haiku-5-5"], "secs": 12.0}